h `checkWinningLease` turned off, the problem case (probe 15) comes back as `{standard, no source}` at all four entry points: `LoadProfile`, `Projector.Project`, `SetProfile`'s from-end and `axpane.deriveProfile`. All 8 of the tests written for this pass there.\n- **The design is sound.** Every new lease after the first records a checkpoint, and an event from an earlier lease only counts if that checkpoint covers it. Events under a lease epoch that was never created, and events when there are no leases at all, fall back to the Session Record. If the checkpoint can't be read, derivation refuses rather than guessing.\n- **The registry entry points at the right code.** I decoded it: the §2.4 \"losing-lease or ambiguous\" clause lists this Story's case, and its owner is `internal/sessprofile/authority.go:Derive`.\n- **Checks are clean.** Build, `go vet` (including the Windows target) and gofmt all pass, and `task-board.config.json` is byte-identical to the base.\n\n**P1 — nothing in the normal test suite would catch a regression.**\n- All 8 tests for this property skip themselves in the committed tree. They only run in a copy with the append gate disabled.\n- I weakened the check so that events from any known lease count again, which brings the original bug back. The normal suite gave 0 failures. So 0 of the 4 entry points have a test that runs in CI and fails under that change.\n- This can be tested with the append gate on. My probe: lease A records a checkpoint, then adds a `profile.changed`, and lease B takes over from that earlier checkpoint. The candidate handles it correctly, and the probe fails under my weakened check.\n- The registry's case lists only tests that always skip.\n\n**P2 — a mutant in an existing test script no longer matches the code.** `N-profile-closure` in `internal/axpane/mutant_harness.py` still looks for the fields this change removed. Running it prints `ERROR: patch anchors 0, want 1`, so that check no longer measures anything.\n\nThe rework 